  "body": "## What changed\n\n**Stacked on #624** (issue #611): it adds a row to the same shipped-machine list. Merge #624 first.\n\nThis adds the **Tormach 15LX Slant-PRO**, one of the lathes PathPilot Hub lists, from the contributor's operator manual **UM10860 §3.1**:\n\n| | 15LX Slant-PRO |\n|---|---|\n| X / Z stroke | 10\" / 14\" |\n| Spindle | max 3500 rpm. The manual states no minimum (servo spindle), so none is stated in the file. |\n| Power | 6 hp continuous ≈ 4.5 kW (the 10 hp peak isn't used, since the machine check judges sustained power) |\n| Feed / rapid | 360 IPM |\n| Tools | 99: gang tooling is standard, and the 8-position turret is a kit |\n\n- **Conventions:** inch, `kind: lathe`, full stroke either way of the work zero, the same as the 8L and 15L in #624.\n- **Why 3500 rpm here but 2500 on the 15L:** this manual gives one maximum, while the 15L's gives a separate 2500 rpm figure for its chuck.\n- **Decision record:** appended to `docs/decisions/611-tormach-lathes.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\n- **`tormach_lathes`, 2/2,** now covering three lathes. A spec with no stated minimum asserts `spindle_min == None`.\n- **Other suites:** machine 32 (the shipped list names the 15LX), tormach_machines 5, tormach_safe_retract 4.\n- **`cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -D warnings`:** clean.\n- No golden or snapshot changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nA Hub run on the 15LX. That needs the PathPilot lathe post, #626.\n\nChangelog: Tormach 15LX Slant-PRO ships as a lathe machine, from its operator manual (#619)\n\nFixes #619\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n\n",
